WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.080
In the last years of the Northern and Southern Dynasties, power in the Northern Zhou fell into the hands of the minister Yang Jian.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:17.486
In the year 581, the Northern Zhou emperor yielded the throne to Yang Jian, who founded the Sui dynasty and became Emperor Wen of Sui.

00:00:17.836 --> 00:00:22.828
After Emperor Wen took the throne, he reorganized the government and established new systems.

00:00:23.178 --> 00:00:26.898
The officials each did their own duty, and the court ran in good order.

00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:31.760
He readied the army, preparing to attack the Chen dynasty in the south.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:35.710
The soldiers trained day and night, their morale high.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:42.804
In the year 589, the Sui army destroyed the Chen dynasty, and China was reunified.

00:00:43.154 --> 00:00:47.018
The people of north and south alike longed for days of peace.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:53.800
Though the Sui dynasty was short-lived, it laid an important foundation for the later golden age of the Tang dynasty.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.014
A reunified China welcomed new hope.

